# Connecting a client

The server speaks two transports. Pick by **who** is connecting:

| Transport | Who uses it | How it's launched |
|-----------|-------------|-------------------|
| **streamable HTTP** | MCP Inspector, remote clients | the container (`dude up`) serves it on `:8000/mcp/` |
| **stdio** | Claude Desktop, Claude Code | the client spawns `python -m app` itself |

---

## MCP Inspector (debugger, no LLM)

The official protocol debugger — list/call tools, read resources, render prompts,
watch raw MCP traffic. No API key.

```bash
docker compose --profile dev up --build
```

Open <http://localhost:6274>, choose Transport **"Streamable HTTP"**, and connect to:

```
http://fastmcp:8000/mcp/
```

(The Inspector proxy reaches the server over the compose network by its service
name, `fastmcp`.)

---

## Claude Desktop (chat, stdio)

Claude Desktop spawns the server itself over **stdio**, so it does not use the
running container — it runs the Python package directly. Provision the venv once:

```bash
cd fastmcp && uv sync
```

Then add the server to
`~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "{{projectName}}": {
      "command": "<ABSOLUTE_PATH>/fastmcp/.venv/bin/python",
      "args": ["-m", "app"],
      "env": {
        "MCP_TRANSPORT": "stdio",
        "PYTHONPATH": "<ABSOLUTE_PATH>/fastmcp"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Replace `<ABSOLUTE_PATH>` with the absolute path to this project. Restart Claude
Desktop; the tools appear under the 🔧 icon.

!!! warning "Use the venv's Python, not `uv run`"
    Claude Desktop does not honour a `cwd`, so `uv run` resolves the wrong
    interpreter and you get `No module named app`. Point `command` straight at
    `fastmcp/.venv/bin/python` and set `PYTHONPATH` to the `fastmcp/` folder.

!!! note "Local stdio servers need `command`, not `url`"
    The `{"url": "…"}` form is only for remote servers added via claude.ai. A
    locally-run server must be configured as a `command` (stdio) entry.

---

## Claude Code (chat, stdio or HTTP)

stdio (spawns the package):

```bash
claude mcp add {{projectName}} \
  --env MCP_TRANSPORT=stdio \
  --env PYTHONPATH="$PWD/fastmcp" \
  -- "$PWD/fastmcp/.venv/bin/python" -m app
```

or HTTP (against the running container — `dude up` first):

```bash
claude mcp add {{projectName}} --transport http http://localhost:8000/mcp/
```
